        "subject": "LU-20596 tests: discover peer after the NI add",
        "message": "LU-20596 tests: discover peer after the NI add\n\nsetup_health_test() discovers the remote peer before it adds a second\nNI to that peer. The local peer record then holds one NI.\n\nlnet_health_check() sets attempt_remote_resend to false when the peer\nholds one NI. LNet then does not resend the message after a remote\nfailure. The first remote_* ping of test_233 fails with -EIO and no\nresend.\n\nDiscover the peer again after the code adds the NIs. Check that the\nlocal peer record holds all remote NIs. Only the multi-rail path adds\nNIs, so keep the single-rail tests on their previous path. Clean up\nthe remote NI when a check fails, because the test exits in a subshell\nand cleanup_health_test() does not run again.\n\nFixes: 3166a201e0a5 (\"LU-15398 tests: Use remote peers for health tests\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5\nChange-Id: Ib4c4ae0a4f962149e09a652fac6ea5a9f4838382\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68297\nReviewed-by: Cyril Bordage <cbordage@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Xinxia Qu <xqu@ddn.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
